renting-vs-buying.html:
  252      <h2>The opportunity cost most comparisons get wrong</h2>
  253:     <p>If you rent instead of buying, the down payment you would have spent doesn't just sit there. Invested in a diversified index fund at a historical ~7% average return, a $50,000-60,000 down payment can grow to roughly $60,000-130,000+ over 5-10 years — the same compounding math covered in our <a href="/simple-vs-compound-interest.html">simple vs. compound interest guide</a> and our <a href="/how-much-down-payment.html">down payment deep-dive</a>. This is real money that a pure "rent vs. mortgage payment" comparison completely ignores, and it's often the deciding factor over shorter time horizons.</p>
  254    </div>

